# Bilingual Content (en + ar)

The site is fully bilingual. English lives at the root path, Arabic at `/ar`. There is no such thing as an English-only or Arabic-only change to user-visible content.

## Rules

- Every key added to `messages/en.json` MUST be added to `messages/ar.json` in the same structure, and vice versa. The two files must have identical key sets.
- Every docs page is a pair: `content/docs/<section>/<page>.mdx` (English) + `content/docs/<section>/<page>.ar.mdx` (Arabic). Never create one without the other.
- Arabic is not a translation afterthought: write natural Arabic a merchant would say, keeping the codebase's light Egyptian flavor. Never machine-translate literally.
- English brand and technical words stay as-is in Arabic copy: Cashvio, POS, USB, QR, CSV.
- Keep interpolation placeholders (`{year}`, `{count}`) and `•` separators identical across both languages.
- Keywords arrays in page files are per-locale: `Record<Locale, string[]>` with both `en` and `ar` filled in.

## Verification

After any content change, confirm key parity (the seo-preflight skill has a script for this). A missing Arabic key throws at runtime with next-intl.
